---
import Page from '../../layouts/ContentPage.astro';import sectors from '../../data/use-cases.json';
export function getStaticPaths(){return sectors.map(s=>({params:{sector:s[0]},props:{s}}))}
const {s}=Astro.props;const faq=[{question:'Is this a published client result?',answer:'No. This is a hypothetical workflow to explain a possible assessment scope. No customer, measured result or sector endorsement is claimed.'},{question:'What is needed before testing?',answer:'Agree the workflow, target system, rules, risks, authorised test data/access, success criteria, stakeholders and constraints. Submission does not authorise testing.'}];
---
<Page title={`AI assurance for ${String(s[1]).toLowerCase()}.`} description={`Assess a defined ${String(s[1]).toLowerCase()} workflow against the rules and outcomes that matter. Use controlled scenarios to examine capability, boundaries and operational behaviour, then review the evidence and exclusions. The example below describes a possible test scope; it is not a measured result or a claim of certification.`} eyebrow="Illustrative sector workflow" faq={faq}>
<h2>What is the problem?</h2><p>{s[4]}</p><h2>Example: {s[2]}</h2><p>{s[3]}</p><h2>What could be tested?</h2><ul>{(s[5] as string[]).map(v=><li>{v}</li>)}</ul><h2>What evidence could you receive?</h2><p>{s[6]}</p><h2>What are the limits?</h2><p>{s[7]}</p><h2>What should you prepare?</h2><p>Describe the workflow and target, the rules and risks, authorised test data or access, success criteria, stakeholders and timing or budget constraints. Use high-level public descriptions until a private scoping channel is agreed.</p><div class="ak-actions"><a class="ak-btn" href="/apply/">Discuss this workflow ↗</a><a class="ak-btn outline" href="/use-cases/">All use cases ↗</a></div></Page>